4. DEALERSHIP PROFILE, DEALER GROUPS AND PRODUCTS
---------------------------------------------------------------------
4.1 Dealership profile fields (captured during scouting and visits, editable on the record, included in import)
- Dealership type: Standalone OR Part of a Dealer Group.
- Number of rooftops.
- Number of used cars (used vehicle inventory count), with an optional monthly used vehicle sales figure. Keep a history so changes over time are visible.
- F&I system in use: dropdown from an editable list managed by owners in Settings, plus "Other" (free text). Record the date captured and the source (asked at visit, researched, etc.).
- Optional: franchise brand(s), or Independent.
- Time zone (auto from ZIP).

4.2 Dealer groups
- A Dealer Group entity (name, HQ address, main decision maker, notes). Each dealership (rooftop) links to its group. The group page shows all rooftops, their stages, products and owners.
- Origin-rep attribution stays PER ROOFTOP.
- When one rooftop signs, flag its sister rooftops as warm opportunities and alert the relevant reps and managers.
- If one group's rooftops span several reps' territories, a manager can set a group-level account owner without changing rooftop attribution or incentives.

4.3 Products (one catalog drives everything)
- Product catalog in Settings: name, category, description, price or pricing model, whether it's restockable (e.g. key fobs / keychains), unit and unit price, and an active/inactive status.
- Track products per dealership across the lifecycle:
  1. INTERESTED at scout time: which products, with interest level (Low / Medium / High).
  2. SIGNED UP for: products in the contract, with sign-up date, price/plan and who signed.
  3. UPSELL: each upsell is its own mini-opportunity (Identified → Pitched → Interested → Won / Lost) with owner, value and next step, and its own Kanban board.
  4. RESTOCK: for restockable products, log every restock (date, quantity, unit price, total $, handled by). Show history, average quantity, frequency, predicted next restock date and total restock revenue.
- Product summary on each record (Interested / Signed / Upselling / Not offered yet), so the gaps are visible at a glance.
- Everything above is filterable and searchable: type, group, rooftops, used inventory size, F&I system, product status and restock status.

