10. DATA LAYER: GOOGLE SHEETS AS THE DATABASE
---------------------------------------------------------------------
- Build a data-access layer (repository pattern) with one interface and three adapters:
  (1) LocalStorage: demo/offline mode with seed data and a "Reset demo data" button
  (2) Google Sheets: the primary storage for real use
  (3) a stub for a future proper database (e.g. Firestore / Cloud SQL)
  Select the adapter in Settings → Data Storage, which shows the active mode.
- Recommended connection: a Google Apps Script web app bound to the spreadsheets as a JSON API, using LockService for safe concurrent writes. Write the full Apps Script code and the deployment steps. Also document the direct Sheets API + OAuth alternative.
- Spreadsheets (one per domain, one tab per entity):
  - CRM_Core: Prospects, Clients, Contacts, Dealer_Groups, Products (catalog), Dealership_Products, F&I_Systems
  - CRM_Activity: Visits, Calls, Notes, Tasks, Workspace_Activity
  - CRM_Pipeline: Stage_History, Claims, Handoffs, Signups, Onboarding_Checklists, Upsells, Restocks
  - CRM_Finance: Incentives, Payouts, Finance_Reviews (shared only with finance + owners)
  - CRM_Gamification: Points_Ledger, Badges, Challenges, Leaderboard_Snapshots
  - CRM_Admin: Users, Roles, Regions, Settings, Audit_Log, Sync_Log
  - CRM_Archive_[YEAR]: old activity moved here yearly
  - CRM_Reporting: read-only summary tables refreshed weekly for the Executive Desk (Looker Studio-ready)
- Data rules:
  - A fixed header row per tab matching a documented schema. Output the schema as a table: tab | column | type | required | example.
  - Every row has a UUID, created_at/by, updated_at/by and a version number. Relationships use IDs, never names.
  - Soft deletes only. Audit_Log is append-only.
  - Optimistic concurrency, with a friendly "someone else updated this" prompt.
  - Batch reads and writes, in-app caching, and an offline write queue for reps with poor signal.
  - Respect quotas (back off and retry); show sync status and errors in the UI.
  - Validate in the app, and add data validation and protected ranges in the sheets.
- A one-click Apps Script setup that creates all spreadsheets, tabs, headers, validation, protection and sharing in a chosen Shared Drive folder. Plus: a connection test, demo seed import, CSV export, and a weekly backup to a dated folder.
- Document the practical limits of Sheets (cell limits, quotas, concurrency, no transactions), roughly when to move to a real database, and how the adapter makes that move easy.

